     08. /31 vs /30
-------------------------
Class C /31 Subnet   
Let’s say we’ve been allocated Class C 200.15.10.0/24.  
 We subnet using /31. 
 Valid host addresses:   200.15.10.0 to 200.15.10.1  
                        200.15.10.2 to 200.15.10.3   
                        Etc., to:   
                        200.15.10.254 to 200.15.10.255

>> For the CCNA exam, use /30 when a subnet to support 2 hosts is required, unless told to use /31
>> Use a /31 subnet for point-to-point connections between 2 hosts when you need to maximize your address space and avoid wasting IP addresses.





